Third-party code attributions
===============================================================================

Cell value/text heuristics and merged-cell write semantics
------------------------------------------------------------

`xgen_seepage/_cellfmt.py` (the `maybe_number` / `cell_text` functions) and the
merge-cell anchor/redirect semantics in `xgen_seepage/live_adapter.py`
(`MergedCellWriteError`, `allow_merge_redirect`) are adapted from:

  PlateerLab/document-adapter
  https://github.com/PlateerLab/document-adapter
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

The adapted logic covers only the cell-value-typing heuristic (deciding
whether a string should be written to Excel as a number or kept as text) and
the merged-cell write-protection pattern. The COM/xlwings live-workbook
access layer itself is original to this project: document-adapter operates
on closed files via openpyxl; xgen-seepage's `live_adapter.py` operates on
the currently open, in-memory Excel application instance, which has no
equivalent in document-adapter.

CSV encoding auto-detection strategy
-------------------------------------

The encoding-detection order in `xgen_seepage/csv_adapter.py`
(`detect_bom` / `detect_encoding`: BOM signature check, then a preferred
encoding, then `chardet` with a confidence threshold, then a fixed candidate
list, then a `latin-1` fallback that always succeeds) is adapted from:

  PlateerLab/xgen-doc2chunk
  https://github.com/PlateerLab/xgen-doc2chunk
  (xgen_doc2chunk/core/processor/csv_helper/csv_encoding.py)
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Login and agent-tool-bridge wire protocol
-------------------------------------------

`xgen_seepage/connector/` (`hash.py`, `auth.py`, `bridge.py`) independently
re-implements, in Python with no code copied, the wire protocol documented by
reading:

  PlateerLab/xgen-connector
  https://github.com/PlateerLab/xgen-connector
  (src/core/hash.ts, src/core/auth.ts, src/core/client.ts, src/main/mcp-bridge.ts)
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Specifically: the `/api/auth/login` request/response shape and the
SHA-256-hex password-hashing requirement (`hash.py`/`auth.py`), and the
`/api/tools/ws/connector-mcp/{user_id}` WebSocket frame protocol: `hello`/
`ping` client frames and `ready`/`mcp_call` server frames, answered with
`mcp_result` (`bridge.py`). xgen-seepage does not depend on xgen-connector at
runtime and does not require it to be installed; only the protocol shape
(endpoint paths, JSON field names, message types) was confirmed by reading
that project's source, not copied from it.

TLS exception for private/self-signed certificates
------------------------------------------------------

The `allow_private_certificate` behavior in `xgen_seepage/connector/
connection_security.py` (used by `http_client.py` and `bridge.py`) serves the
same purpose as:

  PlateerLab/xgen-connector
  https://github.com/PlateerLab/xgen-connector
  (src/main/connection-security.ts: shouldAllowPrivateCertificate,
  xgenWebSocketTlsOptions)
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Only the intent (let a user explicitly trust a closed-network XGEN server's
private CA) was ported; the implementation differs because xgen-connector's
Electron shell can reach multiple origins and therefore scopes the exception
by hostname, while xgen-seepage's HTTP/WebSocket clients are single-purpose
(only ever talk to the one configured server), so a client-wide TLS relax
achieves the same scoping structurally.

